  "id": "Compound::DB00959 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Methylprednisolone is linked to Abcb1 through a mechanism involving the binding of prednisone, a glucocorticoid, to the transporter. This relationship is supported by multiple paths that demonstrate a causal chain from Methylprednisolone to Abcb1 via Prednisone, which binds to the transporter. The presence of a common ancestor, Therapeutic Glucocorticoid, and a shared pathway involving 3-Oxo-Delta(1),Delta(4)-Steroid further reinforces the biological relevance of this interaction. The evidence suggests that Methylprednisolone may modulate Abcb1 activity, potentially influencing drug efflux or cellular homeostasis. The consistent binding of prednisone to Abcb1 across different pathological outcomes, such as Central Serous Retinopathy, Scleral Thinning, and Steroid Withdrawal Syndrome, indicates a broader role in cellular response to glucocorticoids. The mechanistic link is supported by the presence of a well-documented mode of action, with the binding of prednisone to Abcb1 being a key component of the pathway.",
